    <node id="越国">
      <data key="d0">越国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 越国 (Yue State) refers to a historical kingdom that was ruled by 越王勾践 (King Goujian of Yue). This kingdom is notable for its longstanding rivalry with the neighboring 吴国 (Wu State), which was characterized by deep-seated enmity. 越国 is recognized as the domain of King Goujian, who is a significant figure in Chinese history, particularly known for his resilience and eventual victory over Wu.

The kingdom is also associated with notable historical figures such as 范蠡 (Fan Li), who was a strategist and advisor to King Goujian, and is often linked to the military forces of 越国. The state is depicted as a place where cultural exchanges occurred, as illustrated by the mention of 阿青 (Aqing), who engaged in swordsmanship training with warriors from 越国. 

Geographically, 越国 was situated near 吴国, sharing similar customs and traditions, which further highlights the cultural dynamics between these two states. The descriptions collectively emphasize 越国's significance in the context of its historical conflicts, cultural contributions, and notable personalities associated with its legacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-013870c1938481d1558d4c2e439c83d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66</data>
