    <node id="吴国">
      <data key="d0">吴国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 吴国 (State of Wu) was an ancient Chinese state known for its skilled warriors and significant military prowess, particularly in its conflicts with the neighboring state of 越国 (State of Yue). The state was ruled by 吴王夫差 (King Fu Chai), who was noted for his reliance on the capable strategist 伍子胥 (Wu Zixu), contributing to the state's strength and influence during his reign.

吴国 was characterized by its martial culture, with its swordsmen being particularly renowned for their combat abilities. The state engaged in various military confrontations with 越国, marking a period of rivalry and hostility between the two entities. Notably, the state was involved in significant battles, including instances where its swordsmen confronted adversaries such as 阿青 (A Qing) on the streets, showcasing the martial spirit and the ongoing conflicts that defined its historical narrative.

Under the leadership of 吴王夫差, 吴国 experienced a period of prosperity and military success, largely attributed to the strategic insights provided by 伍子胥. This era was marked by the state's aggressive posture against 越国, solidifying its reputation as a formidable power in ancient China. The ongoing enmity with 越国 was a defining feature of 吴国's history, influencing its political and military strategies throughout its existence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71</data>
